.TH LIL 1 "August 2025" "lil" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lil \- a Rust-based shell-to-LLM helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lil
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lil
is a rewrite of the bash-based ell tool in Rust. It provides a set of utilities to interact with Large Language Models (LLMs) from your shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pipe
Pipe any text to
.B lil pipe
to send it to an LLM as a prompt.
.TP
.B record
Start a new recorded shell session. The session will be saved to a log file.
.TP
.B interactive
Start an interactive session with the LLM. Uses the session log file as context.
.TP
.B doctor
Check for common environment issues and dependencies.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B lil
can be configured by creating a
.I lil.toml
file at
.I ~/.config/lil/lil.toml
.SH SEE ALSO
The original project: https://github.com/simonmysun/ell
